It is a solution to a problem that has best been described in an essay by M=
ark Shoulson on the wiki:
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=3DThe%20Case%20Against%20LA

Basically, proficient Lojban speakers have proven unable to prevent the sli=
p-up where the strings =93la=94 or =93doi=94 accidentally appear in nonce n=
ames.

We call the variant of Lojban with all cmevla delimited with pauses on both=
 sides =93dot side=94, in a reference to Star Wars.

> and what (aside from 'lo') is wrong (or was) with gadris.

Well, AFAIK the only serious problem with the Lojban gadri system as descri=
bed in CLL is that it did not allow for intensional descriptions, or non-di=
stributive plurals. The majority of people who voted on the gadri section i=
n BPFK were of the opinion that Lojban couldn't remain without any kind of =
expressing intensional descriptions, so =93lo=94 was pressed into service a=
s an article with unspecified intensionality/extensionality.

The pre-publication drafts of the book =93Plural Predication=94 by Thomas M=
cKay was highly influential in this solution. (http://www.amazon.com/Plural=
-Predication-Thomas-McKay/dp/0199278148/)

